From ff7d1748a54c5c3ea7e15eab759a85a6bc227a2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:08:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] UI-FIT: the text-fit gate in make test, and the hits it
 found

A unit test measures every string of the shared screens in its real box at 240x160
and 320x240, in English and every ready language pack, and fails on overflow, a cut
word, or text covering a button, arrow or other text (docs/UI_TEXTFIT.md). Registration
API core/include/doomo/textfit.h (TEXTFIT_SCREEN) so other streams add their screens.
On the gate: Options, shop, title, pause, and a source scan of every ui_hint,
ui_confirm, ui_title and fixed-width ui_button literal. No resident byte: the
enumerators are compiled only with DOOMO_TEXTFIT (native build).

First run 24 hits (6 in English), all fixed: the confirm window measured its text at
w-20 and drew it at w-24 (ui_modal.c); the Studio's Raise the curtain button 7 px
narrow (cross-stream: studio_stage.c, 120 -> 132 wide); the title's Theme row 23 px
narrow at 240x160 (120 wide at any size); the Options tab Accessibility (now Access)
ran past the arrow at 320x240; 17 Spanish strings shortened (Options labels, hints,
the Slider range help, shop tabs, Coming soon, fishing and dream hints).

Core tests 1467 -> 1472 passed, 0 failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xd63czLgdbSn871LSJKjVC
